    "answer": {
      "short": "\\$40 000 in sales per week.",
      "worked": "Let $x$ be the weekly sales in dollars. Using $\\text{Pay}=\\text{Retainer}+\\text{Percentage}\\times\\text{Sales}$, equate the two payments:\n$$\\begin{align*}600+0.02x&=0.035x\\\\600&=0.015x\\\\\\frac{600}{0.015}&=x\\\\40\\,000&=x\\end{align*}$$\nWilliam needs sales of \\$40 000 per week.",
